d 'FFRALS': module to provide Flexible-Fourier LM unit-root test with RALS and factor (RALS2) augmentation  for non-normal errors
d
d	ffrals implements the flexible-Fourier LM unit-root test of
d Lee, Islam, Tieslau, Payne	and Nazlioglu, in which an unknown
d number of smooth structural breaks is approximated by    a single
d Fourier frequency (chosen by minimum residual sum of squares over
d 1..fmax) and	  the score-based LM statistic is computed by
d augmented regression. With rals(1) the    regression is augmented
d by the residual-augmented least squares (RALS) terms, which	
d exploit non-normality of the errors to gain power without
d nuisance parameters. With    rals(2) the regression is further
d augmented by supplied common and group factors() (the    RALS2
d factor test), making the test robust to cross-sectional
d dependence when applied    series-by-series to a panel. 
d
d KW: unit root tests
d KW: Fourier
d KW: normality
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260726
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
